description:
FILED s506 (Fable, 2026-10-04) from a review probe of s501t (#155 tie); PRE-EXISTING on main e5d72352 with NO tie involved (identical on main and on the s501t tree).  Sibling of #1241 (the plain RVALUE read `my $v = $h{a}{b}` -- fixed s473b with p-viv-container) and of #1058 (the lvalue / `++` spelling): the ARGUMENT position was left out.

PROBE (~/pcl-agent-scratch/s506/review/min/l1.pl, out/l1.perl vs out/l1.base):
  sub wr { $_[0] = "W"; 1 }  sub rd { defined $_[0] ? $_[0] : "undef" }
  my (%p, @q);
  print "viv-h: ", wr($p{nv}{q}), " ", ref($p{nv}), " ", $p{nv}{q} // "undef", "\n";
  print "viv-a: ", wr($q[2][1]), " ", ref($q[2]), " ", $q[2][1] // "undef", "\n";
  print "rd-viv: ", rd($p{zz}{q}), " ", (exists $p{zz} ? "viv" : "no-viv"), " ", rd($q[5][0]), " ", scalar(@q), "\n";
  my $r; print "viv-r: ", wr($r->{a}{b}), " ", ref($r), " ", ref($r->{a} // ""), " ", $r->{a}{b} // "undef", "\n";

  perl 5.40.3            PCL main e5d72352
  viv-h: 1 HASH W        viv-h: 1  undef          <- the write is lost, $p{nv} never created
  viv-a: 1 ARRAY W       viv-a: 1  undef
  rd-viv: undef viv undef 6   rd-viv: undef no-viv undef 3   <- a READ-only callee: perl still vivifies the intermediate
  viv-r: 1 HASH HASH W   viv-r: 1 HASH  undef     <- the ROOT ref is vivified, the middle level is not

WORKS today (do not break): one level (`wr($h{new})`), and a nested element whose intermediate EXISTS (`wr($h{x}{y})` with $h{x} = {}).

CAUSE (read, not yet measured): p-gethash-argbox / p-aref-argbox -- the LAZY @_ accessors -- answer `(make-p-box (p-gethash hash key))`, a DETACHED box, when their container operand is undef ("undef container / special markers / symbolic-ref strings: keep plain value semantics, no aliasing").  perl`s rule (perlref; #1241`s text): every level of a multi-level subscript EXCEPT the last vivifies, also in an argument; the LAST level is deferred (PVLV defelem: created only if the callee assigns).  So the fix is probably the emitter marking the INNER container operands of an argbox chain with p-viv-container / p-viv-array-container (the #1241 mechanism, which the chain walker already expands) -- measure whether the argbox path goes through that walker first; the last level keeps its defelem.
THE TIED TWIN: through a tied container the same shape is wrong the same way on the s501t tree (`wr($tied{nv}{q})`: no STORE(nv), write lost; r506-nested2 row 25) -- re-probe it after the plain fix (perl FETCHes nv, gets undef, vivifies a hash and STOREs it).
BAR when built: corpus-diff (emission change expected in every file that passes a nested element to a sub -- common), bench rows nested / nestedref / arrhash / passarr with a control (argument passing is a hot path: a 50 % compile budget is not the constraint here, RUN time is), sweep + op/ companion leg, ir-conform (the #1241 corpus cases 045-060 have argument-position siblings to add).
Not a queue-jumper by the s411 rule (no baseline regresses, no phase is blocked); a correctness-batch candidate -- ASK the USER before opening one (s494/s498).
